#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Measure of the enforcer.  Usage: check <build-dir>

Runs `<build-dir>/enforce <tree-dir>` against fixture trees: real git
repositories generated in a temporary directory from ONE clean template.
Every case is one line of CASES below: a name, the rule that must be named
(None: the tree is clean and must give exit 0), and how the tree differs from
the clean one.  A breach must give exit 1 and a stdout line starting with
`<rule-id> `.  All pass: exit 0, last stdout line = bytes of the build.
Any fail: exit 1, failing case names on stderr.

The clean tree (see build_tree):

    root.md principles.md queue.md build verdict measure/ ledger.tsv
    judge/stands.tsv              not a unit: only the judge's list
    tool/                         unit, src, "stood unjudged" in record.md
    shop/                         unit, src, stands by stands.tsv (2nd line)
    shop/cat/                     unit, src, stands by stands.tsv, context 4 KB
    shop/kennel/dog/              unit under a plain directory, no src
    decoys that are NOT units: unit.md under measure/, audit/, src/, .cache/
"""
